# .NET Clean Architecture

- Domain: entities, value objects, domain events — no EF, no HTTP, no external SDKs.
- Application: use-cases, handlers, DTOs, validators, repository interfaces.
- Infrastructure: EF Core, external APIs, CAP/RabbitMQ, file storage.
- Host/API: controllers, DI wiring, middleware only.

## Do
- Depend inward (Host → Application → Domain).
- Put business rules in Domain/Application, not controllers.
- Use Result / typed errors instead of throwing for expected failures.

## Don't
- Don't reference Infrastructure from Domain.
- Don't put SQL or DbContext usage in controllers.
- Don't invent new folder layouts without an ADR.
